  "query_preview": "..(This Afternoon Through Saturday)\nIssued at 1152 AM MDT Sun Aug 30 2026\n\nUpper air analysis depicts upper shortwave over northern \nID/southern SK. Water vapor imagery shows line of convection \ndeveloping over central MT/WY and moving eastward. These storms \nwill move into the CWA in the next several hours. Inverted-V \nsoundings indicate damaging wind gusts will be the main concerns \nwith these storms. Some gusts over NW SD could exceed 75+ mph. \nRight now, there's some uncertainty as to how far south these \nstorms will extend and if they'll impact the Rapid City area. \n\nBroad upper level ridge builds over the central/eastern half of \nthe US for the beginning of the week. This will lead to continuing\nwarm conditions over our CWA and mostly dry conditions, though \nafternoon storms are possible tomorrow and Tuesday. Deterministic \nmodels show the ridge strengthening later in the week, leading to \nmuch warmer conditions over western SD and northeastern WY with \nhighs climbing into the mid to upper 90s by Wednesday and \nThursday. In addition to the hot temperatures, the very dry \nairmass will lead to elevated to near-critical fire weather \nconcerns.",
